+# The Daily Grind
+
+The static page loads `coffee-card.js` as a browser module. Each `<coffee-card>`
+owns its markup, styles, rendering, and event listeners in an open shadow root.
+Existing coffee cards retain their content and destinations.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card name="Latte" description="Creamy oat milk."
+  href="/menu/latte" price="4.50" featured></coffee-card>
+```
+
+Attributes and matching JavaScript properties update each other and the rendered
+card immediately:
+
+| Attribute / property | Type | Default / behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `name` | String | Empty string; displayed as the heading |
+| `description` | String | Empty string; displayed as plain text |
+| `href` | String | Empty string; relative and HTTP(S) destinations enable navigation |
+| `price` | Number or `null` | Optional USD amount; `null` removes the attribute |
+| `featured` | Boolean | False; attribute presence means true, even `featured="false"` |
+
+Prices must be finite and nonnegative. Invalid or empty numeric attributes hide
+the price and read as `null`; invalid property assignments throw `RangeError`.
+String setters use `String(value)`. Boolean setters use `Boolean(value)` and
+add or remove the attribute.
+
+On connection, the element replays properties assigned before registration,
+renders, and attaches its click listener. Disconnection removes the listener;
+reconnection restores it. Activating the details link emits a bubbling, composed,
+cancelable `coffee-select` event containing `{ name, href, price, featured }`.
+Calling `preventDefault()` on that event cancels navigation.
+
+Run the automated DOM tests with `pnpm install` followed by `pnpm test`.
